[ ] Decide how the spec represents the grounded domain $FOR THE HUMAN. Recommended: the spec represents V5 directly. Core projects every workspace straight to the CCO/IAO graph in docs/domain.md of the ontology; the spec states the mapping from each DSL, charter and objective field to its V5 pattern and ships SHACL shapes for that output (Decision 42); the CLI's saved queries are rewritten against V5 with their row shapes unchanged, so nvim does not notice; the v4 namespace is retired. Rejected: a compact ClearHead graph plus a published mapping to V5 (mints a vocabulary, against Decision 1, and two graphs to keep in sync); dropping RDF from the query path (gives up meaning in data). Cost: the graph is wordy, about 12 triples for an action with a priority, a context and an energy, and saved queries grow to match; the competency queries in ontology v5/queries are the working templates. The JSON-LD context stops being a contract: it cannot create the extra nodes V5 needs, so JSON-LD is serialized from the graph instead. Derived, overrule if wrong: blocked means waiting on something outside the data, a Performance Specification whose condition is the outside event; scheduled and due times are conditions too; the workspace vocabulary ws (source file and line) is not domain meaning and stays for now, with a search for standard terms planned before it is kept. Two related choices are queued separately: what plus-tags mean, and the root charter objective. Yes closes this and opens the implementation charter.$ !1 +human ^2026-09-30T16:03 <urn\:uuid\:01a0f48f-400c-706b-9dce-d6717b17588c #01a0f48f-4037-76ab-900b-9f2418ad04ec
[ ] Move the SHACL shapes and JSON-LD context into the spec; the ontology keeps only meaning $Per platform Decision 42: move ontology/v4/actions-shapes-v4.ttl and actions.context.json into specifications/schemas beside the JSON schemas, with the examples that test shape and their tests; repoint specifications/ontology.md (which today names ontology/v4/* canonical). Delete ontology/v4/actions.schema.json: a stale second copy (2026-08-18, its own \$id) of the spec's pinned actions.schema.json, and the two differ. Examples that test meaning stay in the ontology. REVISED 2026-10-01: do not move the v4 files as they are. Moving them would put v4 meaning, which V5 retires, into the spec. If the representation decision lands as recommended, this becomes: write SHACL shapes for the V5 output in specifications/schemas, drop the JSON-LD context as a contract, repoint specifications/ontology.md at ontology docs/domain.md, and delete the v4 copies with the rest of v4. It then belongs in the implementation charter.$ !2 ^2026-09-30T21:55 <01a0f48f-4037-76ab-900b-9f2418ad04ec #01a0f5d0-ebb2-73bd-a381-d8e4ae301f9c
[ ] Finish the ROBOT gate\: lint, CI, and retire the Python tests $Per ontology Decision 1. Done 2026-09-30: v5/Makefile (merge, HermiT reason, robot verify, competency queries), pinned imports, pre-push hook. Left: robot report lint on our files; run the gate in CI (the pre-push hook is local only); retire the pyshacl/pytest suite once v4 is gone. Known: v4 plus its examples is inconsistent under HermiT (is_successor_of on actions; status measured backwards); reason over a separately merged file, since chaining merge and reason gave a false green. ADDED 2026-10-01: make test checks that the competency queries run, not what they answer; an empty or wrong answer passes. Add expected answers beside the queries, for example v5/queries/expected/cqN.csv, and fail on any difference, so the eight questions are tests and not just queries that ran.$ !2 ^2026-09-30T21:59 #01a0f5d4-c03c-71b5-ad32-5befd2bfc86d
[ ] Decide what a plus-tag means\: context only, or also topic $FOR THE HUMAN. The DSL's plus-tag is meant as a GTD context, and V5 makes a context a condition: where, with what, or by whom an action can be done (Performance Specification). In practice tags are also topics: +wasm says what the action is about, not when it can be done, and would be mis-stated as a condition. Recommended: a plus-tag means context only, and the spec says so; a topic is what a charter or plan is for, so +wasm work belongs in a plan, and +human stays a context, since it says who can do it. Alternative: a second syntax for topic tags, mapped to a Descriptive ICE about the action; more surface, and topics overlap with charters.$ !2 +human ^2026-10-01T20:16 #01a0fa9d-6f37-7009-ac4e-a1770d1cfdc6
[ ] Confirm how the root charter gets its objective $FOR THE HUMAN. V5 is strict: a plan without an objective is not a plan, and every charter is a plan, the root included. You said: a plan without an objective is just people daydreaming. Recommended, for the spec: a charter's Done when section counts as its objective; init seeds the root charter a maintained objective once, as it seeds the root alias, editable afterward; a charter with no objective is a gap that doctor reports, never a refusal to load. Charter frontmatter already has an objectives field linking objective files; both routes count.$ !2 +human ^2026-10-01T20:16 #01a0fa9d-6f47-7228-a7b1-c64d9e57fba5
